From: theodotdot <59372255+theodotdot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:29:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] screenbrightnessutil: watch the PowerDevil service, not the
 interface

The watcher listens for org.kde.Solid.PowerManagement.Actions.BrightnessControl, an interface name nothing owns, so a PowerDevil that starts after plasmashell is never seen and the quick-settings brightness slider stays hidden for the whole session.

Watch org.kde.Solid.PowerManagement, the service PowerDevil owns. QDBusAbstractInterface::isValid() follows the owner, so the existing brightnessAvailableChanged signal reaches QML when it appears or goes away.
---
 components/screenbrightnessplugin/screenbrightnessutil.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/screenbrightnessplugin/screenbrightnessutil.cpp b/components/screenbrightnessplugin/screenbrightnessutil.cpp
index 2f79a7b..fb5c2a8 100644
--- a/components/screenbrightnessplugin/screenbrightnessutil.cpp
+++ b/components/screenbrightnessplugin/screenbrightnessutil.cpp
@@ -27,8 +27,8 @@ ScreenBrightnessUtil::ScreenBrightnessUtil(QObject *parent)
     fetchBrightness();
     fetchMaxBrightness();
 
-    // watch for brightness interface
-    m_brightnessInterfaceWatcher = new QDBusServiceWatcher(QStringLiteral("org.kde.Solid.PowerManagement.Actions.BrightnessControl"),
+    // Watch the service PowerDevil owns; the interface name is never owned.
+    m_brightnessInterfaceWatcher = new QDBusServiceWatcher(QStringLiteral("org.kde.Solid.PowerManagement"),
                                                            QDBusConnection::sessionBus(),
                                                            QDBusServiceWatcher::WatchForOwnerChange,
                                                            this);
